/ ============================================================================
// LEVEL 1: DENY ALL DEFAULT LAX PATTERNS
// ============================================================================
#![deny(clippy::all)]
#![deny(clippy::pedantic)]
#![deny(clippy::nursery)]
#![deny(clippy::cargo)]

// ============================================================================
// LEVEL 2: CORE ECOSYSTEM ISOLATION (ANTI-CORE LEAK)
// ============================================================================
#![deny(clippy::alloc_instead_of_core)]       // Bans any accidental allocation layers
#![deny(clippy::std_instead_of_core)]         // Guarantees absolute hardware/freestanding code block
#![deny(clippy::std_instead_of_alloc)]        // Enforces total reliance on the core primitives only

// ============================================================================
// LEVEL 3: ZERO RUNTIME PANIC MATRICES (MATHEMATICAL SAFETY)
// ============================================================================
#![deny(clippy::unwrap_used)]                 // Hard-bans .unwrap() panic vectors
#![deny(clippy::expect_used)]                 // Hard-bans .expect() panic vectors
#![deny(clippy::indexing_slicing)]            // Outlaws raw arr[i] access. Requires boundary verification (.get())
#![deny(clippy::panic)]                        // Eliminates the usage of the panic!() macro compile-branches
#![deny(clippy::todo)]                         // Traps and blocks unfinished code hooks
#![deny(clippy::unimplemented)]                // Prevents compile-execution traps
#![deny(clippy::unreachable)]                  // Eradicates unprovable logical dead ends

// ============================================================================
// LEVEL 4: BIT-LEVEL SECURITY & ANTI-SIDE-CHANNEL CASTING
// ============================================================================
#![deny(clippy::as_conversions)]               // Outlaws the "as" operator to strictly eliminate unchecked integer truncation/wraparound
#![deny(clippy::cast_lossless)]                // Enforces compile-time explicit safety on type extensions
#![deny(clippy::cast_possible_truncation)]     // Drops compilation if an integer bit-width can shrink implicitly (e.g., u32 to u8)
#![deny(clippy::cast_possible_wrap)]           // Blocks any type casting that could invert mathematical parity signs
#![deny(clippy::float_arithmetic)]             // Zero tolerance for float non-determinism. Forces strict discrete integer math

// ============================================================================
// LEVEL 5: COMPILER RESTRUCTURING & MEMORY TRACKING
// ============================================================================
#![deny(clippy::missing_inline_in_public_items)] // Mandates explicit #[inline] on public API entries for global LTO analysis
#![deny(clippy::exhaustive_structs)]           // Forces structs to explicitly define all fields to prevent uninitialized memory tricks



### 1. Mathematical Formal Verification & SMT Solvers
* Kani Rust Verifier (`kani`) — Mathematical model checking across all assembly paths to prove zero out-of-bounds states.
* Creusot — Deductive verification via mathematical contracts directly inside the source, using Z3/Why3 solvers.
* AORAI — Automated verification of temporal state and memory properties at the compiler intermediate level.

### 2. Hardcore Static Analysis & Paranoia Lints (Top of lib.rs / main.rs)
* `#![no_std]` — Complete removal of the standard library and dynamic heap allocations, locking everything into the stack.
* `#[deny(unsafe_code)]` — Absolute zero-tolerance ban on raw pointers and unsafe memory operations.
* `#[deny(clippy::pedantic)]` — Enforcement of strict, rigid academic programming structures and security checks.
* `#[deny(clippy::panic, clippy::todo)]` — Complete elimination of compiled crash branches or unhandled panics.
* `#[deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used)]` — Mandatory error propagation via Result; prevents unhandled execution states.
* `#[deny(clippy::indexing_slicing)]` — Outlaws raw array indexing (arr[i]). Forces safe boundary resolution (.get()) over raw arrays.

### 3. Automated Chaos, Fuzzing & Coverage Suites
* cargo-fuzz (`libFuzzer`) — Real-time injection of billions of malformed binary payloads to discover logical edge-cases.
* Proptest — Property-Based generation to challenge invariant stability and verify mathematical invariants under stress.
* cargo-tarpaulin — Code coverage engine to guarantee strict 100% path execution testing across the entire system.
* Loom — Permutation analyzer ensuring zero memory synchronization races under concurrency loads.

### 4. Microarchitectural Shielding & Side-Channel Defenses
* dudect-bencher — Statistical constant-time verifier using Welch's t-test profiles to prove immunity against execution time leakage.
* cargo-show-asm — Visual assembly validator to verify the elimination of runtime execution branches.
* Speculative Execution Mitigation — Assembly-level hardware fences (LFENCE) injected to block CPU cache snooping (Spectre/Meltdown).

### 5. Production Profile Optimization Matrix (Cargo.toml)
* opt-level = 3 — Enforces maximum machine code vectorization and processing speed.
* lto = true — Aggressive link-time optimization for dead-code elimination across the dependency graph.
* codegen-units = 1 — Monolithic optimization context for absolute global scope analysis.
* panic = "abort" — Immediate process termination on anomaly, wiping memory trace states instantly.
* strip = true — Complete removal of binary symbols, debug tracks, and metadata for total anonymity.

### 6. Compilation Layer Verification
* Ferrocene Compiler — ISO 26262 / IEC 61508 safety-certified downstream Rust compiler to guarantee zero microcode compiler errors.
